{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror","id":1196014,"title":"Psychological Horror","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-16T05:18:03-07:00","id":1196014,"title":"Psychological Horror","content":"So, I've been thinking about psychological horror in Chronicles of Darkness and I think it would be a good fit. Chronicles of Darkness is very much about personal horror and psychological horror fits in this category very well. What I'm thinking of specifically are monsters like those in Silent Hill combined with other elements of psychological horror.<br /> <br /> So, later on today, I'm going to post some monsters that represent elements of some of my characters' psychology. The first character is an Invictis Ventrue who seeks out power because he is terrified of unchecked chaos, both as a vampire and as something that was once human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T06:46:22-07:00","id":1196031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror#post1196014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've been thinking about psychological horror in Chronicles of Darkness and I think it would be a good fit. Chronicles of Darkness is very much about personal horror and psychological horror fits in this category very well. What I'm thinking of specifically are monsters like those in Silent Hill combined with other elements of psychological horror.<br /> <br /> So, later on today, I'm going to post some monsters that represent elements of some of my characters' psychology. The first character is an Invictis Ventrue who seeks out power because he is terrified of unchecked chaos, both as a vampire and as something that was once human.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, Goetia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:51:22-07:00","id":1196051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1196031#post1196031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, Goetia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits spawned by a character's psychoses would fit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T07:55:21-07:00","id":1196053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1196051#post1196051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirits spawned by a character's psychoses would fit too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose it would depend on the desired focus, really - Spirits are great for examining the repercussions of one's actions on the environment, and Goetia for their impact and shaping of individuals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T08:52:05-07:00","id":1196079,"title":"","content":"Okay, I didn't actually know what Goetia were because I didn't know that much about mage but upon researching it, I think it and the psychoses spirits are the perfect fit. Thanks to everyone who gave me the idea. I'll have to alter the Goetia a little bit to make them fit better or, in the very least, give a reason why these spirits are manifesting on this vampire specifically instead of others. So, I'll have to do more research.<br /> <br /> But, in the meantime, here is the most powerful being the vampire has spawned:<br /> <br /> The Crawling Chaos: This spirit's name is intentional, as the vampire's fear of chaos came, in part, from his readings of Lovecraft. It is not a full spirit of chaos, but a manifestation of the vampire's fear of what chaos brings. As a result, it is not ever-shifting, as most Idigams are (though Idigams aren't exactly spirits of chaos).<br /> <br /> The form of the Crawling Chaos is a giant darkness with arms that burst from it to drag targets in to be consumed.<br /> <br /> Rank: 4.<br /> Power: 12.<br /> Finesse: 4.<br /> Resistance: 10.<br /> Max. Essence: 25.<br /> Size: 6.<br /> Corpus: 16.<br /> Willpower: 14.<br /> Initiative: 14.<br /> Defense: 4.<br /> Speed: 10.<br /> Ban: Is killed if its current target overcomes their fear of chaos.<br /> Bane: Takes aggravated damage from a sword weighed in scales and dipped in the blood of a lawmaker.<br /> Influences:<br /> Chaos: 2.<br /> Murder: 1.<br /> Destruction: 1.<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Forms, Materialize, Shadow Gate-Way, Reaching, and Possess.<br /> Numina: Aggressive Meme, Awe, Implant Mission, Telekinesis, Firestarter, Dement, Emotional Aura, and Hallucination.<br /> <br /> Note that this entity is intended to be more of a force of nature than a standard opponent. Until the character overcomes their fear, they can't do much against it other than flee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T12:43:31-07:00","id":1196175,"title":"","content":"Um, how powerful is this Invictus to have his psychosis spawn a Rank -4- spirit. Those guys are usually spirits of small cities, infamous charnel houses, pervasive regional trends and other big stuff<br /> <br /> A Rank 4 Goetia is more reasonable, though you'd have to have a reason for it to have all those manifestations they usually need a Mage to get","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 03-16-2018, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-16T17:25:16-07:00","id":1196294,"title":"","content":"Rank 4? Is the Ventrue in question perhaps an elder (the ones in TYoN, old enough to have a transformed clan curse), and the spirit his ages-old nemesis?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:37:16-07:00","id":1196477,"title":"","content":"This Ventrue is an elder. He was designed to be the potential sire of one of the player characters. Or, if not that, then the prince of the city they are in. The idea is that his actions spawned a bunch of horrible spirits that his children and city have to deal with.<br /> <br /> His fear of chaos did not directly spawn the spirit. The actions he took as a result of his fear of chaos did. And he did some pretty horrible things to prevent chaos. To put it simply, if the other vampires found out what he did, he wouldn't remain Prince for very long. And I fully expect the player characters to orchestrate his downfall once they find out about it. He is powerful enough that he could defeat them easily, but he isn't invulnerable and he has plenty of enemies.<br /> <br /> The spirit is a nemesis of his. It has been following him around and destroying everything he creates.<br /> <br /> Thank you all for your input. I'll probably end up stating him out before moving on to another character, but remember that his emotions indirectly spawned the spirits. His actions were more what spawned them, influenced by his emotions.<br /> <br /> And no, before you ask, he is not a Nazi and never was.<br /> <br /> Without further ado, here is one of the types of weaker, and more common, spirit's he's spawned:<br /> <br /> Spirit of Control: These spirits are the polar opposite of the Crawling Chaos. They are the vampire's love of order and his ruthlessness in pursuing it. Their forms are vaguely militaristic, though what country they come from is indistinct.<br /> <br /> Rank: 1.<br /> Power: 3.<br /> Finesse: 1.<br /> Resistance: 3.<br /> Corpus: 4.<br /> Willpower: 4.<br /> Initiative: 4.<br /> Defense: 1.<br /> Speed: 9.<br /> Size: 1.<br /> Ban: It must pick up any small objects it drops.<br /> Bane: Spray paint (a symbol of anarchy).<br /> Influence: Control 1.<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form and Reaching.<br /> Numina: Aggressive Meme and Telekinesis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T07:39:39-07:00","id":1196479,"title":"","content":"Okay, I reread the Crawling Chaos with more scrutiny and, yeah, I messed up. He is powerful but not enough that his emotions alone could have spawned that spirit, which is what I wrote down. So, feel free to ignore that bit, and perhaps the spirit entirely, if you use it in your own games. Thank you all for pointing out my mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T09:04:10-07:00","id":1196505,"title":"","content":"Hmm. I wonder what would happen if the Goetia for their psychosis got out of their head and tried eating the Spirits generated by those emotions (or the opposite). They'd need a Numina to let them interact with the other type (like Ghost Eater does), but it <i>might</i> work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T09:29:26-07:00","id":1196511,"title":"","content":"OMG! That is an amazing idea! I'll look into it and post what I've come up with tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T12:34:09-07:00","id":1196562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1196505#post1196505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm. I wonder what would happen if the Goetia for their psychosis got out of their head and tried eating the Spirits generated by those emotions (or the opposite). They'd need a Numina to let them interact with the other type (like Ghost Eater does), but it <i>might</i> work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it extremely rare for goetia to be in the material plane, shadow or otherwise and not in the astral without a mage having had conjured there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-17T12:41:24-07:00","id":1196564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1196562#post1196562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isn't it extremely rare for goetia to be in the material plane, shadow or otherwise and not in the astral without a mage having had conjured there?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes*. So? Rare implies uncommon, yet not impossible. It's probably also rare for Goetia and Spirits to eat each other. Again, not impossible. The impossible becomes <i>guaranteed</i> with the weight of plot necessity.<br /> <br /> * Unless you are running a setting that does away with that constraint via house-rule, as I often do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T12:42:56-07:00","id":1196879,"title":"","content":"Ok, I had something come up and I wanted to let people know that the goetia will be a day late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T14:43:53-07:00","id":1196907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1196879#post1196879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I had something come up and I wanted to let people know that the goetia will be a day late.</div> </div> </div> </div>Take your time - no one here is putting you on a deadline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T10:57:48-07:00","id":1197264,"title":"","content":"Thanks and do you know where I can find resources for making goetia? The research is taking a bit longer than I thought it would.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T13:35:49-07:00","id":1197314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xela_nut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1197264#post1197264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks and do you know where I can find resources for making goetia? The research is taking a bit longer than I thought it would.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So far, they are just in Mage: the Awakening (2E). Goetia are ephemeral, like Spirit, but they lack Manifestations (typically - I house-rule otherwise, but that is a deviation from the listed rules), and so require other forces (like Mages) to grant them such so they can interact with the material world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T14:05:49-07:00","id":1197325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1196014-psychological-horror?p=1197314#post1197314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So far, they are just in Mage: the Awakening (2E). Goetia are ephemeral, like Spirit, but they lack Manifestations (typically - I house-rule otherwise, but that is a deviation from the listed rules), and so require other forces (like Mages) to grant them such so they can interact with the material world.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're in the Beast Player's Guide as well, where they're called Dreamborn; that book highlights something that's only noticeable by inference in Mage's copy of the ephemeral being mechanics, which is that they only have as many dots of Influence as their Rank and cannot trade Numina for more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T11:23:14-07:00","id":1197689,"title":"","content":"Ok, I have a Goetia:<br /> <br /> The All-Consumer: Mass murder and destruction, for a long time they were the vampire's trademarks. Anyone who was a threat to his order died, or so he thought. One of the people he killed was the lover of a mage. The mage decided that death was too good for the vampire and reached deep into his mind with magic, unleashing a Goetia. This Goetia is the vampire's desire for power personified. It follows the vampire to consume the ghosts of his victims and increase its own strength. Eventually, it seeks to find another mage so it can gain the power to permanently possess the vampire.<br /> <br /> Rank: 2.<br /> Power: 5.<br /> Finesse: 2.<br /> Resistance: 3.<br /> Corpus: 5.<br /> Willpower: 5.<br /> Initiative: 5.<br /> Defense: 2.<br /> Speed: 12.<br /> Size: 2.<br /> Ban: Must consume a ghost once per month.<br /> Bane: Is vulnerable to anti-corruption books and pamphlets.<br /> Influence: Power 1 and Desire 1.<br /> Manifestations: Twilight Form and Materialized.<br /> Numina: Ghost Eater, Implant Mission, Emotional Aura, and Omen Trance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T12:01:05-07:00","id":1197697,"title":"","content":"Once again, thank you all for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23983-xela_nut","name":"xela_nut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"91"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}